KG42.register("rules-540d04f054a877bfec2297c4",{"id":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R003","paper":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R003","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03-lem","name":"Demand submission","process_stage":"bidding","market_meaning":"Prosumers may generate buying-quantity bids within assigned DOEs and submit their chosen trading bids to the LEM in each τ. Scope: Prosumer buying-quantity submissions for peer and upstream-grid trading under the proposed bidding strategy. Condition: When a prosumer chooses buying/imports. Peer and upstream-grid buying quantities must each be nonnegative and no greater than the assigned import DOE; their combined quantity must not exceed that DOE. Scope: Buying quantities selected by the prosumer bidding strategy in each time-slot. Condition: The assigned import DOE P̂_{j,t} > 0. Demand bids are chosen within a total-trading-cost minimization that accounts for purchase costs and sale profits from trading with peers and the upstream grid. Scope: Demand-quantity decisions within the proposed joint buying/selling bidding optimization.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function bidding.demand under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.demand"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Buying quantities selected by the prosumer bidding strategy in each time-slot. | Demand-quantity decisions within the proposed joint buying/selling bidding optimization. | Prosumer buying-quantity submissions for peer and upstream-grid trading under the proposed bidding strategy.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E30","v141-b-g02-E33"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R003-x-Ppb","symbol":"P^{pb}_{j,t}","meaning":"Total peer-to-peer buying-quantity bid of prosumer j at time t.","kind":"operational","domain":"real buying quantity (power); under P̂_{j,t}>0, 0 ≤ P^{pb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t} by Eq. (31)","unit":null,"indices":["j","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E33"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R003-x-Pgb","symbol":"P^{gb}_{j,t}","meaning":"Upstream-grid buying-quantity bid of prosumer j at time t.","kind":"operational","domain":"real buying quantity (power); under P̂_{j,t}>0, 0 ≤ P^{gb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t} by Eq. (33)","unit":null,"indices":["j","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g02-E30"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-theta-DOE","symbol":"P̂_{j,t}","meaning":"Assigned dynamic operating envelope (DOE) for prosumer j at time t; this demand-submission rule uses the positive import-DOE branch P̂_{j,t}>0.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"assigned DOE; condition P̂_{j,t} > 0 for the import/demand branch"},"unit":null,"indices":["j","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E30"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Prosumers may generate buying-quantity bids within assigned DOEs and submit their chosen trading bids to the LEM in each τ. Scope: Prosumer buying-quantity submissions for peer and upstream-grid trading under the proposed bidding strategy. Condition: When a prosumer chooses buying/imports.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Peer and upstream-grid buying quantities must each be nonnegative and no greater than the assigned import DOE; their combined quantity must not exceed that DOE. Scope: Buying quantities selected by the prosumer bidding strategy in each time-slot. Condition: The assigned import DOE P̂_{j,t} > 0.","expression":"∀j∈J, ∀t∈T: P̂_{j,t} > 0 ⇒ (0 ≤ P^{pb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t}) ∧ (0 ≤ P^{gb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t}) ∧ (P^{pb}_{j,t} + P^{gb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t})","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-x-Ppb","v141-c-R003-x-Pgb"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-theta-DOE"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E30","v141-b-g02-E33"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Demand bids are chosen within a total-trading-cost minimization that accounts for purchase costs and sale profits from trading with peers and the upstream grid. Scope: Demand-quantity decisions within the proposed joint buying/selling bidding optimization.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E27","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"Prosumers Bidding Strategy","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON SMART GRID, VOL. 15, NO. 2, MARCH 2024 lem tou lem ad min Ppbj,t · j,t + Pgbj,t","equation_id":"(28)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Prosumers can decide on their participation in the P2P trading or trading with the upstream grid by generating their bids for buying/selling energy within DOEs. Each prosumer decides on the trading bids and submits them to the LEM in each τ by the proposed bidding strategy. In this case, the objective of prosumer is to minimize the total trading cost as, min ∑_{j∈J} (P^{pb}_{j,t}·Λ^{lem}_{j,t} + P^{gb}_{j,t}·Λ^{tou}_{j,t} + P^{ps}_{j,t}·Λ^{lem}_{j,t} + P^{gs}_{j,t}·Λ^{fit}_{t}) τ; P^{ps}_{j,t}, P^{gs}_{j,t} ≤ 0, ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, subject to: (29)−(35), (28) where the first and second terms in (28) refer to the total cost of buying energy from the peers and the upstream grid, respectively and the third and fourth terms define the total profit of selling energy to the peers and the upstream grid in the LEM, respectively. Here, P^{pb}_{j,t}/P^{ps}_{j,t} and P^{gb}_{j,t}/P^{gs}_{j,t} are buying/selling quantities of prosumer j with the peers and the upstream grid in each τ, respectively; and Λ^{tou}_{j,t} are the time-of-use (ToU) buying prices with the upstream grid."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E28","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p07-c2r2__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"Prosumers Bidding Strategy","anchor_text":"p y , j,t j,t j,t j,t y g g quantities of prosumer j with the peers and the upstream grid Vs- in eac","equation_id":"(29)-(30)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Prosumers are allowed to trade in the LEM within the assigned DOEs P̂_{j,t} confirming the network-constrained operation. The sum of the buying energy of prosumer j at time t with the peers and the upstream grid should be equal to or less than the DOE limits P̂_{j,t}(> 0), and the sum of the selling energy with the peers and the upstream grid should be equal to or greater than the DOE limits P̂_{j,t}(≤ 0) as in (29) and (30), respectively. P^{pb}_{j,t} + P^{gb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} > 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, (29) P^{ps}_{j,t} + P^{gs}_{j,t} ≥ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} ≤ 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T. (30)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E29","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"Prosumers Bidding Strategy","anchor_text":"1, in each τ is constrained by (31), which is not greater than 6), Pj,t(> 0), and the total P2P sell","equation_id":"(31)-(32)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The total P2P buying quantity P^{pb}_{j,t}(> 0) for each prosumer in each τ is constrained by (31), which is not greater than P̂_{j,t}(> 0), and the total P2P selling quantity P^{ps}_{j,t}(\u003c 0) for each prosumer in each τ is limited by P̂_{j,t}(≤ 0) as in (32). 0 ≤ P^{pb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} > 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, (31) P̂_{j,t} ≤ P^{ps}_{j,t} ≤ 0, if P̂_{j,t} ≤ 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T. (32)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E30","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"Prosumers Bidding Strategy","anchor_text":"1, in each τ is constrained by (31), which is not greater than 6), Pj,t(> 0), and the total P2P sell","equation_id":"(33)-(34)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"On the other hand, constraints (33) and (34) limit the buying quantity P^{gb}_{j,t} and the selling quantity P^{gs}_{j,t} in each τ with the upstream grid, respectively. It is assumed that if no P2P trade occurs, the trade with the grid should be equal to the DOE but it is less than the DOE when there is a P2P trade. 0 ≤ P^{gb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} > 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, (33) P̂_{j,t} ≤ P^{gs}_{j,t} ≤ 0, if P̂_{j,t} ≤ 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T. (34)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E33","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M03-matching","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"P2P Trading Mechanism","anchor_text":"HOQUE et al.: DOE-BASED LEM FOR PROSUMERS WITH EVs by prosumer j ∈J from (to) prosumer i ∈J |i̸ = j.","equation_id":"(36)-(37)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The single P2P buying energy P^{pb}_{j,i,t} is limited by P^{pb}_{j,t} and the single P2P selling energy P^{ps}_{j,i,t} is constrained by P^{ps}_{j,t} as in (36) and (37), respectively, where P^{pb}_{j,t}/P^{ps}_{j,t} is the buying/selling quantity bid of prosumer j at a time t as in Section V-B. Prosumer j can only trade energy with prosumer i at time t as stated in (36) and (37), where C_{j,i,t} is a binary variable to represent the P2P trading status such that C_{j,i,t} = 1 if prosumer j buys energy from prosumer i. 0 ≤ P^{pb}_{j,i,t} ≤ P^{pb}_{j,t} C_{j,i,t}; ∀(j,i) ∈ J | j ≠ i, ∀t∈T, (36) P^{ps}_{j,t}(1 − C_{j,i,t}) ≤ P^{ps}_{j,i,t} ≤ 0; ∀(j,i) ∈ J | j ≠ i, ∀t∈T. (37)"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M03-bidding","v141-a-M03-matching","v141-a-M03-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"bidding.demand","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E27","quote":"Prosumers can decide on their participation in the P2P trading or trading with the upstream grid by generating their bids for buying/selling energy within DOEs. Each prosumer decides on the trading bids and submits them to the LEM in each τ by the proposed bidding strategy."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E28","quote":"P^{pb}_{j,t} + P^{gb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} > 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, (29)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E29","quote":"0 ≤ P^{pb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} > 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, (31)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E30","quote":"0 ≤ P^{gb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} > 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, (33)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E33","quote":"where P^{pb}_{j,t}/P^{ps}_{j,t} is the buying/selling quantity bid of prosumer j at a time t as in Section V-B."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E27","quote":"Each prosumer decides on the trading bids and submits them to the LEM in each τ by the proposed bidding strategy. In this case, the objective of prosumer is to minimize the total trading cost as,"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E27","quote":"where the first and second terms in (28) refer to the total cost of buying energy from the peers and the upstream grid, respectively and the third and fourth terms define the total profit of selling energy to the peers and the upstream grid in the LEM, respectively."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"80535886c93489b17f240ddc9e7ff3a4b4395158f454a0089931587312b1b373","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The core import-DOE bound in C002 is formalized directly from the source inequalities (31), (33), and (29): each peer and upstream-grid buying quantity is nonnegative and bounded by the positive import DOE, and their sum is bounded by that DOE. C001 remains a procedural bid-generation/submission statement. C003 remains objective context and is not formalized here because Eq. (28) is a joint buying/selling trading-cost objective that spans supply-side terms not present in this demand-only frozen node. The supplied B evidence remains unreviewed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-x-Ppb","node_ids":["bidding.demand"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"P^{pb}_{j,t} is defined in the source as the prosumer's peer buying-quantity bid, which is the demand-submission decision owned by bidding.demand. The frozen rule has no additional edges."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-x-Pgb","node_ids":["bidding.demand"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"P^{gb}_{j,t} is the upstream-grid buying-quantity bid of the prosumer and is constrained as part of the demand submission within the import DOE. The frozen rule has no additional edges."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-theta-DOE","node_ids":["bidding.demand"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The assigned import DOE P̂_{j,t} is an exogenous envelope limit on the prosumer's demand bid; it is bound to bidding.demand because it supplies the positive import bound used by C002."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C002","node_ids":["bidding.demand"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C002 transcribes source equations (31), (33), and (29) for the demand bid node. The frozen graph has no additional edge to attach; these are unary bounds and a combined bound on the bid quantities."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
